Done ΓÇö code changed and task ticked. The commit is pending your approval (all git-write commands are gated in this session).

**What I fixed** ΓÇö the top item, *"HARNESS STILL LYING in two places"* (`game/mocks/ring_vibes.gd`, `--proving` harness). Both were harness faults, not physics:

- **(a) on-road terminal never measured.** `_offroad` was re-derived from live position every frame, so a straight tangent leaving the curving 8m ribbon settled every on-road phase at the *off-road* terminal (box 9.8). Now the course **pins** `_offroad` per phase (`_prove_offroad`): 0 for accel/brake/circle/bumps, 1 for rough/climb, and `_drive_tick` honours the pin while proving. accel now reads the on-road terminal (box ~22, clamped by `top`).
- **(b) bump-strip jolt read ~0.** The jolt metric sampled `_terrain_h` alone ΓÇö the calibrated strip is added via `_proving_surface`, so it never appeared in the jolt column. `h_start` and the loop `h` now add `_proving_surface`; the strip phase is pinned on-road so it carries speed to cross the ramp/drop and potholes in 40s instead of stalling in the washboard.

Not run-verified ΓÇö the Godot binary is out-of-repo/gated here, so no live `--proving`.

To land it, approve this commit (only my two files, leaving the `logs/*` changes alone):

```
git commit -m "fix(proving): pin surface per phase and put the bump strip in the jolt" -- game/mocks/ring_vibes.gd TASKS.md
```

